  "note": "Triennial election of the Ballycastle Urban District Council, polled Wednesday 21 May 1958. Twelve candidates, all Nationalists, were nominated for the twelve seats, so there was no election; Thomas Campbell and Hugh Dempsey were the new members (Northern Whig, 8 May 1958, p. 3). No election; Hugh Dempsey was a new member. Returned unopposed.",
